v><div id='status' class='info-box'>The negation map i ↦ −i swaps which voice is on top.<br>Click any interval on the clock to see if consonance is preserved.</div><script>const names=['P1','m2','M2','m3','M3','P4','A4/d5','P5','m6','M6','m7','M7'];const fullNames=['Unison','Minor 2nd','Major 2nd','Minor 3rd','Major 3rd','Perfect 4th','Tritone','Perfect 5th','Minor 6th','Major 6th','Minor 7th','Major 7th'];const consonant=new Set([0,3,4,7,8,9]);const perfect=new Set([0,7]);const clock=document.getElementById('clock');const cx=225,cy=225,R=170;for(let i=0;i<12;i++){const angle=-Math.PI/2+i*2*Math.PI/12;const x=cx+R*Math.cos(angle)-30;const y=cy+R*Math.sin(angle)-30;const div=document.createElement('div');div.className='note '+(perfect.has(i)?'perfect':consonant.has(i)?'consonant':'dissonant');div.id='note-'+i;div.innerHTML=`<span>${names[i]}</span><span style='font-size:.7rem;opacity:.7'>${i}</span>`;div.style.left=x+'px';div.style.top=y+'px';div.onclick=()=>showSwap(i);clock.appendChild(div)}function showSwap(i){document.querySelectorAll('.note').forEach(n=>n.classList.remove('highlighted'));const neg=(12-i)%12;document.getElementById('note-'+i).classList.add('highlighted');document.getElementById('note-'+neg).classList.add('highlighted');const iCons=consonant.has(i),negCons=consonant.has(neg);const iPerf=perfect.has(i),negPerf=perfect.has(neg);const iClass=iPerf?'perf':iCons?'cons':'diss';const negClass=negPerf?'perf':negCons?'cons':'diss';const pc=document.getElementById('pair-container');pc.innerHTML=`<div class='pair-display'><div class='pair-box ${iClass}'><div style='font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:bold'>${fullNames[i]}</div><div>${i} semitones</div><div style='font-size:.85rem;margin-top:4px'>${iPerf?'Perfect':iCons?'Consonant':'Dissonant'}</div></div><div class='arrow-between'>→ −i →</div><div class='pair-box ${negClass}'><div style='font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:bold'>${fullNames[neg]}</div><div>${neg} semitones</div><div style='font-size:.85rem;margin-top:4px'>${negPerf?'Perfect':negCons?'Consonant':'Dissonant'}</div></div></div>`;const preserved=iCons===negCons;const status=document.getElementById('status');if(i===7){status.innerHTML='<span style=\"color:#ff4444;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:bold\">⚠ COUNTEREXAMPLE!</span><br>The perfect fifth (7) maps to the perfect fourth (5), which is <strong>dissonant</strong> in first-species counterpoint.<br>This proves the consonant set is NOT closed under negation.<br><em>(Theorem: voice_swap_breaks_consonance)</em>'}else if(i===5){status.innerHTML='<span style=\"color:#ff4444;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:bold\">⚠ COUNTEREXAMPLE!</span><br>The perfect fourth (5) is dissonant, but maps to the perfect fifth (7), which is consonant.<br>Consonance depends on which voice is in the bass!'}else if(preserved){status.innerHTML=`<span style=\"color:#44ff44\">✓ Preserved:</span> ${fullNames[i]} (${iCons?'consonant':'dissonant'}) → ${fullNames[neg]} (${negCons?'consonant':'dissonant'})`}else{status.innerHTML=`<span style=\"color:#ff4444\">✗ Broken:</span> ${fullNames[i]} (${iCons?'consonant':'dissonant'}) → ${fullNames[neg]} (${negCons?'consonant':'dissonant'})`}}</script></body></html>"
