      "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang='en'><head><meta charset='UTF-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><title>Voice-Swap Asymmetry</title><style>*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}body{font-family:'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;background:#0a0a1a;color:#e0e0e0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;padding:30px;min-height:100vh}h1{font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:5px;color:#7eb8da}h2{font-size:.9rem;font-weight:normal;color:#888;margin-bottom:30px}.clock{position:relative;width:450px;height:450px;margin:0 auto}.note{position:absolute;width:60px;height:60px;border-radius:50%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:.8rem;font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer;transition:all .3s;border:2px solid transparent}.note:hover{transform:scale(1.15)}.note.consonant{background:#1a3a1a;border-color:#44ff44;color:#44ff44}.note.dissonant{background:#2a1a1a;border-color:#ff4444;color:#ff4444}.note.perfect{background:#3a2a0a;border-color:#ffd700;color:#ffd700}.note.highlighted{box-shadow:0 0 20px rgba(255,255,255,0.5);transform:scale(1.2)}.arrow{position:absolute;pointer-events:none}.info-box{margin-top:30px;padding:20px;background:#1a1a2e;border-radius:12px;max-width:500px;text-align:center;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6}.pair-display{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:20px;margin:20px 0;font-size:1.2rem}.pair-box{padding:12px 20px;border-radius:10px;text-align:center}.pair-box.cons{background:#1a3a1a;border:2px solid #44ff44;color:#44ff44}.pair-box.diss{background:#2a1a1a;border:2px solid #ff4444;color:#ff4444}.pair-box.perf{background:#3a2a0a;border:2px solid #ffd700;color:#ffd700}.arrow-between{font-size:2rem;color:#888}#status{margin-top:15px;font-size:1rem;min-height:60px}</style></head><body><h1>🔄 Voice-Swap Asymmetry</h1><h2>Click an interval to see its negation under i ↦ −i (mod 12)</h2><div class='clock' id='clock'></div><div id='pair-container'></div><div id='status' class='info-box'>The negation map i ↦ −i swaps which voice is on top.<br>Click any interval on the clock to see if consonance is preserved.</div><script>const names=['P1','m2','M2','m3','M3','P4','A4/d5','P5','m6','M6','m7','M7'];const fullNames=['Unison','Minor 2nd','Major 2nd','Minor 3rd','Major 3rd','Perfect 4th','Tritone','Perfect 5th','Minor 6th','Major 6th','Minor 7th','Major 7th'];const consonant=new Set([0,3,4,7,8,9]);const perfect=new Set([0,7]);const clock=document.getElementById('clock');const cx=225,cy=225,R=170;for(let i=0;i<12;i++){const angle=-Math.PI/2+i*2*Math.PI/12;const x=cx+R*Math.cos(angle)-30;const y=cy+R*Math.sin(angle)-30;const div=document.createElement('div');div.className='note '+(perfect.has(i)?'perfect':consonant.has(i)?'consonant':'dissonant');div.id='note-'+i;div.innerHTML=`<span>${names[i]}</span><span style='font-size:.7rem;opacity:.7'>${i}</span>`;div.style.left=x+'px';div.style.top=y+'px';div.onclick=()=>showSwap(i);clock.appendChild(div)}function showSwap(i){document.querySelectorAll('.note').forEach(n=>n.classList.remove('highlighted'));const neg=(12-i)%12;document.getElementById('note-'+i).classList.add('highlighted');document.getElementById('note-'+neg).classList.add('highlighted');const iCons=consonant.has(i),negCons=consonant.has(neg);const iPerf=perfect.has(i),negPerf=perfect.has(neg);const iClass=iPerf?'perf':iCons?'cons':'diss';const negClass=negPerf?'perf':negCons?'cons':'diss';const pc=document.getElementById('pair-container');pc.innerHTML=`<div class='pair-display'><div class='pair-box ${iClass}'><div style='font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:bold'>${fullNames[i]}</div><div>${i} semitones</div><div style='font-size:.85rem;margin-top:4px'>${iPerf?'Perfect':iCons?'Consonant':'Dissonant'}</div></div><div class='arrow-between'>→ −i →</div><div class='pair-box ${negClass}'><div style='font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:bold'>${fullNames[neg]}</div><div>${neg} semitones</div><div style='font-size:.85rem;margin-top:4px'>${negPerf?'Perfect':negCons?'Consonant':'Dissonant'}</div></div></div>`;const preserved=iCons===negCons;const status=document.getElementById('status');if(i===7){status.innerHTML='<span style=\"color:#ff4444;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:bold\">⚠ COUNTEREXAMPLE!</span><br>The perfect fifth (7) maps to the perfect fourth (5), which is <strong>dissonant</strong> in first-species counterpoint.<br>This proves the consonant set is NOT closed under negation.<br><em>(Theorem: voice_swap_breaks_consonance)</em>'}else if(i===5){status.innerHTML='<span style=\"color:#ff4444;font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:bold\">⚠ COUNTEREXAMPLE!</span><br>The perfect fourth (5) is dissonant, but maps to the perfect fifth (7), which is consonant.<br>Consonance depends on which voice is in the bass!'}else if(preserved){status.innerHTML=`<span style=\"color:#44ff44\">✓ Preserved:</span> ${fullNames[i]} (${iCons?'consonant':'dissonant'}) → ${fullNames[neg]} (${negCons?'consonant':'dissonant'})`}else{status.innerHTML=`<span style=\"color:#ff4444\">✗ Broken:</span> ${fullNames[i]} (${iCons?'consonant':'dissonant'}) → ${fullNames[neg]} (${negCons?'consonant':'dissonant'})`}}</script></body></html>"
